cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "notebooklm-kb-system"
message: "If you use this kit, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Aporta Franco"
    given-names: "Fernando"
    alias: ferinazumaDEV
repository-code: "https://github.com/ferinazumaDEV/notebooklm-kb-system"
# Landing page for citation. The DOI, not the repository URL: repository-code above
# already carries the GitHub location, and a repository URL breaks on a rename, an
# account move or a platform migration. The concept DOI does not.
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22554843"
# Concept DOI: resolves to the latest archived release, so it does not change when a
# new version is tagged. Version DOIs live on the Zenodo record page, not here.
# Read from the existing v0.1.0 deposit rather than assumed.
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22554843"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.22554843"
    description: "Concept DOI — always the latest version"
abstract: >-
  A kit of shell scripts that turns a NotebookLM notebook into a queryable knowledge
  base for an agent: build documents from sources, publish them, ask questions from a
  terminal, and degrade to a local copy when the session is not available. It is not
  affiliated with Google, and it is built on an unofficial interface, so anything it
  depends on can change without notice.
# ONE license id here, deliberately, and it is a scalar. A YAML list converts to
# {"id": [...]}, Zenodo rejects the deposit, and the release is archived as Failed
# with no DOI minted. That is not a guess: it is what happened to the cookbook's
# v0.1.0 on 4 Sep 2026, reproduced with cffconvert 2.0.0.
#
# AGPL-3.0-or-later: the licence policy for this cluster's service-with-a-moat, decided
# on 25 August 2026 and applied to this repository on 22 September 2026, when the source
# headers, both READMEs, the FAQ and the provenance notes were all moved to it in one
# change. Until then the repository said "AGPL-3.0" everywhere, which is the "only"
# form. The change is a relaxation — it grants more, not less — made by the sole
# copyright holder. This file follows the repository's declared licence; it never leads it.
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
keywords:
  - notebooklm
  - knowledge base
  - retrieval
  - agent tooling
  - shell
# version and date-released are bumped together with the git tag. The tag is the
# source of truth; these two are the copy the citation format requires.
version: "0.1.1"
date-released: "2026-09-22"
